# Performance Optimization Guide

> **Related Rules**: [Frontend Component Patterns](frontend-component-patterns.mdc) | [GraphQL Integration](graphql-integration-patterns.mdc) | [Component Architecture](component-architecture.mdc) | [TableGrid Advanced Patterns](table-grid-advanced-patterns.mdc)

This guide covers performance optimization strategies for the EduHub application, including frontend optimization, caching strategies, and database performance.

## Frontend Performance Optimization

### React Component Optimization

#### Memoization Patterns
```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Memoize expensive calculations
const CourseStatistics: React.FC<{ enrollments: Enrollment[] }> = ({ enrollments }) => {
  const statistics = useMemo(() => {
    return {
      totalEnrolled: enrollments.length,
      activeEnrollments: enrollments.filter(e => e.status === 'ACTIVE').length,
      completionRate: calculateCompletionRate(enrollments),
    };
  }, [enrollments]);

  return <StatisticsDisplay stats={statistics} />;
};

// ✅ GOOD: Memoize callback functions
const CourseList: React.FC<{ courses: Course[] }> = ({ courses }) => {
  const handleCourseSelect = useCallback((courseId: string) => {
    // Handle selection logic
    onCourseSelect(courseId);
  }, [onCourseSelect]);

  const handleEnrollmentUpdate = useCallback((courseId: string, enrollment: Enrollment) => {
    // Update enrollment logic
    updateEnrollment(courseId, enrollment);
  }, [updateEnrollment]);

  return (
    <div>
      {courses.map(course => (
        <CourseCard
          key={course.id}
          course={course}
          onSelect={handleCourseSelect}
          onEnrollmentUpdate={handleEnrollmentUpdate}
        />
      ))}
    </div>
  );
};
```

